    "EXPLANATORY-CLAIM": [
      {
        "location": "ARCHITECTURE.md:64",
        "text": "## v2.05 Gate 1 safeguards"
      },
      {
        "location": "ARCHITECTURE.md:72",
        "text": "## v2.06 regression-safe structure warnings"
      },
      {
        "location": "ARCHITECTURE.md:102",
        "text": "Task-specific prompt bullets and the old task-name UI audit were removed. Generic checks cover action roles, menu structure, image accessible names, region containment, raw input vs normalized display, exact composite copy, seeds, fixed clocks and persistence. This is intended to improve held-out requirements, not just the six benchmark tasks."
      },
      {
        "location": "ARCHITECTURE.md:106",
        "text": "v2.11's coverage-only gate produced false GREEN results: model-authored specs could mention contract terms while the generated app still missed navigation destinations and regions. v2.12 adds inferred navigation labels and parent/child relations (without task names), exact quoted message extraction, link/heading checks, region containment checks, numeric-threshold warnings, and a minimal behavior-test gate requiring both an action and an assertion. `accept` now blocks missing strict labels, miss"
      },
      {
        "location": "infrastructure/repository/requirements.py:12",
        "text": "raw = yaml.safe_load(document.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\"))"
      },
      {
        "location": "infrastructure/repository/ui_audit.py:1",
        "text": "\"\"\"Generic UI-structure warnings."
      },
      {
        "location": "infrastructure/repository/ui_audit.py:65",
        "text": "\"\"\"Report generic structural risks; warnings never block already passing behavior.\"\"\""
      },
      {
        "location": "README.md:54",
        "text": "`remember` supports a standalone update. A working fact has `text` and either a list of `files` inspected at their current hashes or the path-to-hash map returned in working memory. Supplied hashes are validated. Invalid optional `work` produces a warning and does not block a valid primary action; standalone `remember` and the primary action's own safety/acceptance checks remain strict. Facts are bounded model-authored claims, not independently verified truths. Per-feature working memory persist"
      },
      {
        "location": "README.md:72",
        "text": "Successful checks can be reused within the process by content fingerprints of code, selected tests and imported helpers, fixture/schema, manifests/lockfile, installed tool versions, relevant environment and build outputs. Failures are not cached, and a check that changes its own inputs is rejected as current evidence. Deleted/changed build outputs invalidate build evidence. Reports identify cache hits and actual execution counts. Unknown/dynamic dependencies are treated conservatively; this is n"
      },
      {
        "location": "README.md:113",
        "text": "The v2.12 checkout includes `tests/test_action_schema.py`, `tests/test_contract.py`, `tests/test_ui_audit.py`, `tests/test_browser_result.py` and `tests/test_generic_prompt.py`. They verify action schemas, inferred navigation labels/relations, containment, exact term/status/account/clock extraction, test coverage and behavior diagnostics, structured Playwright failures, and generic UI-structure warnings."
      },
      {
        "location": "README.md:115",
        "text": "The template pins `rollup` to `4.68.7` because the Huawei npm mirror used by the platform does not yet serve `4.68.8`; without the pin, a fresh Vite install resolves the missing latest tarball and fails with E404. v2.12 keeps the blank template and free generation path. It fixes v2.11's false GREEN by extracting unannotated navigation labels/relations and exact messages, checking parent/child links, region containment, exact heading/link rules and numeric threshold copy. Contract coverage now in"
      },
